  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Support to IDP&apos;s in West Darfur</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HAI is currently implementing a multi sectoral programme in 12 IDP camps in West Darfur: Madina Hujaj, Abuzar, Riyad, Krinding I and II, Dorti, and Ardamata in the vicinity of El Geneina, and Gokar, Habillah, Sisi, Krenek and Mornei in rural areas.  The project aims to reach 18,620 older people in these camps, as well as 9,558 people who are expected to benefit from the mobile eye campaigns in four more camps in West Darfur and three in North Darfur. The activities will be as follows:  surgical operation and medical treatment for people with limited vision; geriatric drugs in 7 camps; geriatric training in 3 states; and in all 12 camps the following: referrals to hospital; social centres for older people; income generating activities; shelter; informal education training.  HAI&#x2019;s main office is in El Geneina and two sub offices, one in Mornei IDP Camp - which is the largest camp in West Darfur with more than 61,034 IDPs, and another in Habillah.</narrative>
  </description>
